    <node id="axm:need:build-capability-proof-ladder"><data key="label">The generated spine contains 1,769 capability declarations, while the repository explicitly states that declarations and self-test presence are not runtime proof.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:clarify-offline-first-launch"><data key="label">Offline first launch is not claimed for the public source path, while an offline Windows candidate capability exists separately.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:clarify-snapshot-release-labels"><data key="label">The latest commit is labeled an AXM Workshop v0.5.0 experimental public snapshot while public status documents still name v0.3.0-experimental as the current release.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:import-real-module1-module2-artifacts"><data key="label">Module 3 currently links to Module 1 and Module 2 through explicit placeholder interoperability references rather than ingested implementation artifacts and current handoff records.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:prove-clean-macos-linux-launch"><data key="label">A clean first launch on macOS and Linux is not independently proven.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:refresh-generated-discovery-counts"><data key="label">The pinned README reports 177 modules and 1,183 declared capabilities, while the generated registry at the same commit reports 210 modules and 1,769 declared capabilities.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:reuse-existing-evolution-providers"><data key="label">Several existing modules already provide observation, research, evidence, scheduling, review, diagnostics, recovery, and packaging functions that Module 3 could accidentally duplicate.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:need:run-independent-beginner-comprehension"><data key="label">Independent first-time-human comprehension has not been run.</data><data key="type">IMPROVEMENT_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:research:beginner-comprehension-protocol"><data key="label">What minimal consent-aware beginner trial can test whether a first-time user understands one AXM creation route?</data><data key="type">RESEARCH_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:research:capability-proof-method-selection"><data key="label">Which narrow high-reach capability path should be the first independently reproducible proof-ladder case, and what exact evidence is required?</data><data key="type">RESEARCH_NEED</data></node>
    <node id="axm:research:clean-platform-launch-matrix"><data key="label">What clean-device test matrix distinguishes source bootstrap, bundled offline candidate, macOS, and Linux launch claims?</data><data key="type">RESEARCH_NEED</data></node>
